The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
dma_spec->np = of_parse_phandle(ofdma->of_node, "dma-masters", 0);
if (!dma_spec->np) {
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Can't get DMA master\n");
    return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
}
```
Reason:
The function `of_parse_phandle()` increments the reference count of the node pointer it returns. If the function encounters an error (i.e., `dma_spec->np` is NULL), it returns early without releasing the reference, leading to a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
of_node_put(dma_spec->np);
```
Reason:
The added call to `of_node_put()` ensures that the reference count of the node pointer is decremented when it is no longer needed, preventing the memory leak by balancing the reference count.

